      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s36-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p01.mp3",
      "en": "The dog days, also called sanfu tian in Chinese, refer to the hottest and most humid days of the year.",
      "cn": "酷暑期，在中文里又称“三伏天”，是指一年中最热、最潮湿的日子。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s36-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p02.mp3",
      "en": "This hottest period can be different from year to year.",
      "cn": "这段最热的时期每年是不一样的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s36-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p03.mp3",
      "en": "It starts in July and lasts for about 30 to 40 days.",
      "cn": "它从七月开始，持续大约30到40天。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s36-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p04.mp3",
      "en": "It has three stages: chufu, zhongfu and mofu.",
      "cn": "三伏天有三个阶段：初伏、中伏和末伏。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s36-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p05.mp3",
      "en": "Zhongfu is usually the hottest of the three.",
      "cn": "中伏通常是三个阶段中最热的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s36-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p06.mp3",
      "en": "Because of the high temperatures, people may feel uncomfortable and have a poor appetite.",
      "cn": "由于高温，人们可能会感到不舒服，食欲不振。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s36-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p07.mp3",
      "en": "Some even get sick from eating too many cold foods, like ice cream, watermelons or cucumbers.",
      "cn": "有些人甚至因为吃太多冷食如冰激凌、西瓜或黄瓜而生病。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s36-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p08.mp3",
      "en": "What's more, too much onion can also upset the stomach during the dog days.",
      "cn": "此外，在三伏天里，吃太多洋葱也会引起胃部不适。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s36-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p09.mp3",
      "en": "It is important to choose the proper foods during the dog days.",
      "cn": "三伏天里，选择合适的食物很重要。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s36-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p10.mp3",
      "en": "Foods which are easy to digest and full of protein are good choices, such as vegetables, chicken, eggs, peanuts and tofu.",
      "cn": "蔬菜、鸡肉、鸡蛋、花生和豆腐等易于消化且富含蛋白质的食物都是不错的选择。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s36-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p11.mp3",
      "en": "It's better not to eat uncooked, cold or spicy foods.",
      "cn": "最好不要吃生冷或辛辣的食物。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s36-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p12.mp3",
      "en": "Besides choosing the proper foods, the taste of a dish is also important.",
      "cn": "除了选择合适的食物之外，菜肴的味道也很重要。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s36-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Sour taste can improve the appetite and bitter taste makes people feel refreshed.",
      "cn": "酸味可以增加食欲，苦味则让人神清气爽。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s36-p14-01",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p14-01.mp3",
      "en": "For example, you can enhance the sour flavour by adding a squeeze of lemon,",
      "cn": "比如，你可以挤入一些柠檬汁来增加酸味，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s36-p14-02",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p14-02.mp3",
      "en": "while fresh pepper can give flavour to the food without making it too spicy.",
      "cn": "而新鲜的胡椒能为食物增添风味，又不会让它太辣。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s36-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p15.mp3",
      "en": "As a saying goes, 'Eating a chicken at the beginning of the dog days will keep you healthy for a whole year.'",
      "cn": "俗话说：“头伏一只鸡，一年好身体。”"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s36-p16-01",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p16-01.mp3",
      "en": "Therefore, as soon as the dog days arrive,",
      "cn": "因此，一到三伏天，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s36-p16-02",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s36-p16-02.mp3",
      "en": "it will be better for you to choose proper foods to keep healthy.",
      "cn": "你最好选择合适的食物来保持健康。"
    }
  ]
